ine or button written in ALL CAPS (more than 2 words)?","pushes":"high","fix":"Use sentence case."},{"meter":"ci","id":"ci3","q":"Does any copy use urgency words (now, today, instantly, limited, last, fast)?","yes":"Urgency word present","w":20,"kind":"jev","jev":"Is this true? Does any copy use urgency words (now, today, instantly, limited, last, fast)?","pushes":"high","fix":"Drop the urgency word."},{"meter":"ci","id":"ci4","q":"Does any copy use a superlative or extreme word (best, #1, ultimate, never before, revolutionary, 10x)?","yes":"Superlative present","w":18,"kind":"jev","jev":"Is this true? Does any copy use a superlative or extreme word (best, #1, ultimate, never before, revolutionary, 10x)?","pushes":"high","fix":"Swap for a plain factual claim."},{"meter":"ci","id":"ci6","q":"Is the copy all sentence-case, with no exclamation and no urgency word?","yes":"None of those cues present","w":14,"kind":"jev","jev":"Is this true? Is the copy all sentence-case, with no exclamation and no urgency word?","pushes":"low","fix":"Keep it this way for calm."},{"meter":"ci","id":"ci8","q":"Does the headline use a hedge or soft verb (can, may, helps, supports, gently)?","yes":"Hedge/soft verb present","w":16,"kind":"jev","jev":"Is this true? Does the headline use a hedge or soft verb (can, may, helps, supports, gently)?","pushes":"low","fix":"Keep for calm; say 'helps' not 'transforms'."},{"meter":"ci","id":"ci9","q":"Is the copy free of numbers, percentages and big claims?","yes":"No numeric claim","w":12,"kind":"jev","jev":"Is this true? Is the copy free of numbers, percentages and big claims?","pushes":"low","fix":"Add no number; keep it plain."}]
